# `value instanceof Promise` asks the constructor for @@hasInstance, and the function that it finds on Function.prototype asks the constructor for `prototype`. Both are members that never change,
# so both are answered when the program is built. What is left is the walk up the chain of the value, which a primitive does not come to
# function isWaiting(value) { return value instanceof Promise; }
