# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: [[above]]: builtin(PromisePrototype) @Cell = Builtin builtin=PromisePrototype
# CHECK: = HasInPrototypeChain v0, [[above]]
# RUN(NEVER): walk f1 mechanisms=none+TypedOperations
# NEVER-NOT: = InstanceOf
# The same where the constructor is written as a free name.
# RUN(NAME): walk f2 mechanisms=none+TypedOperations
# NAME-LABEL: code f2:Body
# NAME-NOT: PropGet
# NAME: = HasInPrototypeChain
# Of a constructor that nobody knows both are asked: function isOne(value, constructor) { return value instanceof constructor; }
# RUN(UNKNOWN): walk f3 mechanisms=none+TypedOperations
# UNKNOWN-LABEL: code f3:Body
# UNKNOWN: = InstanceOf v0, v1
# What is no constructor throws, in the words of the operator: function isMath(value) { return value instanceof Math; }
# RUN(OBJECT): walk f4 mechanisms=none+TypedOperations
# OBJECT-LABEL: code f4:Body
# OBJECT: = InstanceOf
# With typed operations withheld the operator stays as it is written.
# RUN(CLOSED): walk f1 mechanisms=none
# CLOSED-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CLOSED: = InstanceOf

